---
// web/src/pages/privacy.astro: privacy + terms (#terms). Needed for Google OAuth verification.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy and terms · Sideload"
  description="What Sideload stores while it moves your Spotify library to YouTube Music, where, for how long, and how to disconnect. No accounts, no analytics cookies."
>
  <section class="container page">
    <p class="eyebrow page__eyebrow">Privacy</p>
    <h1 class="h2">What we keep, and for how long.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Sideload is a transfer tool, not a service you sign up for. It holds what it needs to move your library and then
      lets go of it.
    </p>
    <p class="meta">Updated 4 September 2026.</p>
    <dl class="faq prose">
      <div class="faq__item">
        <dt>What we collect</dt><dd>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <b>Tokens.</b> A Spotify access token (read-only scopes: your library, playlists and followed artists, plus
              your email to show which account is signed in) and a YouTube token (scope <code>youtube</code>: create
              playlists, add songs, like, subscribe). Both are encrypted at rest with a key only the worker holds.
            </li>
            <li>
              <b>Library metadata for the transfer.</b> Playlist names, song titles, artists, albums, durations, and for each
              song what happened to it (moved, needs review, skipped).
            </li>
            <li><b>Your IP address</b>, used only for rate limiting and never stored with a transfer.</li>
            <li>
              <b>Cookies.</b> Two HttpOnly session cookies (<code>sl_s</code>, 1 hour; <code>sl_o</code>, 15 minutes)
              that hold your sign-in state until the transfer starts. No analytics or advertising cookies.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div class="faq__item">
        <dt>Where it is stored</dt><dd>
          <p>
            On Cloudflare, in a Durable Object dedicated to your transfer, encrypted at rest. The service is
            region-agnostic. The shared match cache (below) lives in Cloudflare KV.
          </p>
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div class="faq__item">
        <dt>How long</dt><dd>
          <table class="retention">
            <tr><th>Spotify token</th><td>Deleted the moment the transfer finishes (or fails)</td></tr>
            <tr
              ><th>YouTube token</th><td
                >Kept up to 24 hours after the transfer so you can fix unmatched songs; deleted earlier when you press
                "Disconnect now"</td
              ></tr
            >
            <tr><th>Transfer record</th><td>Deleted 7 days after completion. The link stops working then.</td></tr>
            <tr
              ><th>Match cache</th><td
                >180 days. Contains only "artist · title → YouTube video" pairs, nothing about who moved them.</td
              ></tr
            >
            <tr
              ><th>Logs</th><td
                >7 days. They contain counts and the first 6 characters of a transfer id, never titles, emails or
                tokens.</td
              ></tr
            >
          </table>
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div class="faq__item">
        <dt>Google user data we use</dt><dd>
          <p>
            With the YouTube token Sideload creates the playlists you chose, adds the matched songs to them, likes
            songs, saves albums, subscribes to artists, and reads the new playlists back once to check that every add
            went through. It also reads your channel name to show which account is signed in. It never reads your watch
            history or comments, and never deletes anything.
          </p>
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div class="faq__item">
        <dt>Who we share Google user data with</dt><dd>
          <p>
            Nobody. Your YouTube token, channel name and the video ids written to your account are never sold, rented,
            transferred or disclosed to a third party, never used for advertising, never used to train models, and never
            read by a person. One company processes them on our behalf: Cloudflare, which hosts the service and stores
            the encrypted token for the life of the transfer.
          </p>
          <p>
            Two other services receive server-side data that contains no Google user data. Sentry gets error reports:
            the stack trace and the request path, with cookies and headers stripped, so never a token, a title or an
            account. Mixpanel gets usage counts (playlists in a transfer, songs matched, how long it took) under a
            random per-session id that is not linked to your Google or Spotify account. The page itself runs no
            analytics script and sets no analytics cookie. Spotify only ever sees the read requests for your own
            library.
          </p>
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div class="faq__item">
        <dt>How Google user data is protected</dt><dd>
          <ul>
            <li><b>In transit:</b> HTTPS only, with HSTS, between your browser, Sideload, Google and Spotify.</li>
            <li>
              <b>At rest:</b> tokens are encrypted with AES-256-GCM before they are written. The key is a Worker secret held
              separately from the storage; without it the stored tokens are unreadable.
            </li>
            <li>
              <b>Isolation:</b> each transfer lives in its own Durable Object. Nothing is shared between transfers except
              the anonymous match cache.
            </li>
            <li>
              <b>Access:</b> a transfer page is reachable only through its 128-bit random id, which is never indexed and appears
              in logs only as its first 6 characters. Session cookies are HttpOnly, Secure and SameSite. The only administrative
              access is the author's Cloudflare account, protected with two-factor authentication.
            </li>
            <li><b>Logs and error reports</b> never contain tokens, titles, emails or account names.</li>
            <li>
              <b>Deletion:</b> automatic on the schedule above, or immediately with Disconnect now. Revoking Sideload in your
              Google account invalidates the stored token at once.
            </li>
            <li><b>Code:</b> all of the above is open source and can be checked line by line.</li>
          </ul>
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div class="faq__item">
        <dt>Google API Services</dt><dd>
          <p>
            Sideload's use and transfer of information received from Google APIs adheres to the <a
              href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy"
              rel="noopener">Google API Services User Data Policy</a
            >, including the Limited Use requirements. The YouTube token is used only to create the playlists, likes,
            saved albums and subscriptions you asked for, and to read those playlists back once to verify them. It is
            deleted as described above.
          </p>
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div class="faq__item">
        <dt>Your choices</dt><dd>
          <ul>
            <li>Press <b>Disconnect now</b> on a finished transfer to drop the YouTube token immediately.</li>
            <li>
              Revoke Sideload's access at any time at <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions" rel="noopener"
                >myaccount.google.com/permissions</a
              > and at <a href="https://www.spotify.com/account/apps/" rel="noopener">spotify.com/account/apps</a>. Your
              Spotify app is yours: delete it from the developer dashboard whenever you like.
            </li>
            <li>Questions: <a href="mailto:marctorrelles@gmail.com">marctorrelles@gmail.com</a>.</li>
          </ul>
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div class="faq__item" id="terms">
        <dt>Terms</dt><dd>
          <p>
            Sideload is provided as is, without warranty of any kind, under the <a
              href="https://github.com/marctorrelles/sideload/blob/main/LICENSE"
              rel="noopener">MIT license</a
            >. It copies data into your own accounts at your request and never deletes anything on the Spotify side.
            Matching is automatic and imperfect: check the review list and the CSV report. Sideload is not affiliated
            with Spotify, YouTube, Google, Apple or Tidal. You are responsible for complying with those services' terms
            when you use it.
          </p>
        </dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </section>
</Base>
<style>
  .prose p {
    margin: 0 0 12px;
  }
  .prose ul {
    padding-left: 18px;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .prose li {
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .prose b {
    color: var(--fg);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .prose code {
    font-size: 14px;
  }
  .retention {
    border-collapse: collapse;
    width: 100%;
    font: 400 16px/1.5 var(--font-ui);
  }
  .retention th,
  .retention td {
    text-align: left;
    vertical-align: top;
    padding: 10px 12px 10px 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline);
  }
  .retention th {
    color: var(--fg);
    font-weight: 500;
    white-space: nowrap;
    width: 9em;
  }
  .retention td {
    color: var(--fg-2);
  }
  .retention tr:first-child th,
  .retention tr:first-child td {
    border-top: 0;
  }
</style>
